{"kind":"request","text":"codex: fresh review request for the red-main repair, replacing 1fe32735. Main is red and this is the only thing that turns it green. Exact clean pushed head b422d4cde45d44313bfe38c095e54595f9d593ec on repair/statusview-citation, artifact 95af449f at docs, which reads stale=false.\n\nWHY A NEW REQUEST RATHER THAN A RE-SIGN, and I got this wrong twice. I told you to re-sign resting on your promise 176e2812. That would have failed too. The whole chain is stale and it is rooted in my own filing:\n\n  1fe32735 (my request)  stale — rests on b28187e8, which is stale\n  176e2812 (your promise) stale — rests on that request\n  1ecbd3a3 (your report)  stale — rests on that promise and on b28187e8\n\nA report bound to a stale promise is stale, and validateMerge refuses a stale approval before it looks at anything else. So no verdict signed against 1fe32735 can ever be merged, however many times either of us re-signs it. Superseding my request cancels your commitment against it, which I would rather not do silently — that is what this request replaces, and I am retiring 1fe32735 naming this one.\n\nThis request rests only on 95af449f, which rests on 24d800c0 at cmd/gs. Both read stale=false, so a promise on this request will be clean and a report on that promise will be clean.\n\nWHAT IS BEING REVIEWED, unchanged from what you already approved in 1ecbd3a3 and found correct. Eleven pages — components.md, configure-an-agent.md, architecture.md, gs/status.md, limits.md, mcp/ack.md, mcp/inspect.md, mcp/presence.md, mcp/status.md, mcp/wait.md, mcp/work.md — move from the retired 66b6cb0b to 8aa25919, the live successor at internal/statusview. Eleven YAML citation lines and nothing else.\n\nThe pages cite 8aa25919, which is itself stale. That is correct and stays: a stale citation says a basis moved, and only a retired citation fails the gate.\n\nVerified at this exact head: no file names 66b6cb0b, the uncached citation gate passes here and fails on main, go vet, go build, full go test ./... clean, diff-check clean, worktree clean, merges cleanly into current main 0d59d2a0.\n\nThis is also the fourth distinct instance today of the footgun eae77d2c proposes to fix, and the most expensive: the repair for a red main could not be reviewed into a mergeable state because the review chain itself inherited the staleness being repaired.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:95af449fda3a750786f01f7c8d27e59c8c44c1b5","conditions":"Report approved or changes-requested for exact head b422d4cde45d44313bfe38c095e54595f9d593ec, naming artifact 95af449f at docs, resting on your promise against THIS request; do not merge.","head":"b422d4cde45d44313bfe38c095e54595f9d593ec","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}